<title>USA: St Louis feeder cattle prices up $1-$3 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Louis feeder cattle prices up $1-$3 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>EAST ST LOUIS, Ill. 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>FEEDER CATTLE</p>
<p>AUCTION: 250 head. Compared with last week feeder steers and</p>
<p>heifers were unevenly $1.00-$3.00 per cwt higher, USDA said.</p>
<p>Overall quality was below last week's level. Moderate buyer</p>
<p>attendance. Receipts 250  Last week 250 Last Year  300</p>
<p>FEEDER STEERS: Medium and Large Frame 1:</p>
<p>500-600 lbs. 81.00-88.00, Crossbreds  81.00-88.00</p>
<p>600-700 lbs. 79.00-85.00</p>
<p>Moderately Fleshy:  800-1150 lbs. 61.00-67.00</p>
<p>Large Frame 2 Holsteins: 300-500 lbs. 60.00-64.00</p>
<p>FEEDER HEIFERS:  Medium and Large Frame 1:</p>
<p>500-600 lbs. 74.00-78.00</p>
<p>600-700 lbs. 70.00-75.00</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
